      "message": "At the time I cherry-picked the commit, the equivalent fix from Linux stable was not yet integrated in android-4.19-stable, so the gerrit cherry-picked commit contained changes. While my patch was reviewed, the fix from Linux stable got in android-4.19-stable. After my patch passed review, gerrit applied the commit with --allow-empty.\n\nI agree that gerrit shouldn\u0027t apply individual commits with --allow-empty. Looking into the gerrit docummentation (https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/config-project-config.html#submit.rejectEmptyCommit) I see there\u0027s a submit.rejectEmptyCommit option, but it handles both individual commits and merges with the same option. And allowing merges with empty commits is desirable. It looks like gerrit configuration could be improved.",
